                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "99c3b0d7-e884-4781-aa4f-942cdb32dd74",
                        "entry_id": "916264f2-c5cb-3ed6-90d1-01bb514586cc",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "overscented"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a883e55b-7a92-3fe3-ac0c-db3e59b6de9c",
                        "entry_id": "916264f2-c5cb-3ed6-90d1-01bb514586cc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To give too much scent to (something or someone); to scent excessively."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "911631e6-ae34-4ca9-a8c0-6f9bf4fc625b",
                                "sense_id": "a883e55b-7a92-3fe3-ac0c-db3e59b6de9c",
                                "text": "1989, Dan Bertalan, Traditional Bowyers of America, East Lansing, MI: Envisage Unlimited, Chapter 10, p. 158,\nHe figured the big bear was coming in downwind and picking up his scent. “So I moved the bait station about 200 yards to a better location. Most bear hunters won’t make so many changes because they’re scared of overscenting the area. But I knew I had to make changes to kill that bear. […] ”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f3e34d95-e9c9-4b8d-b457-f8f0c147bc35",
                                "sense_id": "a883e55b-7a92-3fe3-ac0c-db3e59b6de9c",
                                "text": "Licking articles is sometimes seen in an experienced dog when the handler is very nervous, has sweaty palms, and overscents the article."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fac503f1-5127-410b-8171-5ba8e8718196",
                                "sense_id": "a883e55b-7a92-3fe3-ac0c-db3e59b6de9c",
                                "text": "Adding aroma—by having fragrant flowers or flowering plants or using fragrant room sprays or candles—to a lounge/family room is lovely, but don’t overscent the room because it can increase, rather than decrease, tension and cause headaches!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "730b12de-d953-3816-9e89-267237e149e6",
                        "entry_id": "916264f2-c5cb-3ed6-90d1-01bb514586cc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To apply too much scent to oneself."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive",
                            "reflexive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f916e3f6-90e7-445e-96ef-23e0dbdb4636",
                                "sense_id": "730b12de-d953-3816-9e89-267237e149e6",
                                "text": "It is never good taste to overscent one’s-self, but a person who uses no kind of artificial perfume at all, neither in soap nor in pomade, nor yet in the linen, is not always the most agreeable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd5d3bb7-97a0-427a-8454-df204f2ee968",
                                "sense_id": "730b12de-d953-3816-9e89-267237e149e6",
                                "text": "Cologne and perfume are nice but use in moderation. If you overscent, you run the risk that your interviewer dislikes the smell, or even has a bad reaction to it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b9c23d7-f225-4797-b00a-13329e3d20a1",
                                "sense_id": "730b12de-d953-3816-9e89-267237e149e6",
                                "text": "A young lady does not spray herself with so much sun-ripened raspberry body splash that she attracts bees. She particularly does not overscent herself if she is going to be in a confined space with captive companions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "12777175-78e3-45e2-a972-7fc070d3073e",
                                "sense_id": "730b12de-d953-3816-9e89-267237e149e6",
                                "text": "“Just spray in front of you, dear girl,” he advises. “Then walk into the mist. It’s vulgar to overscent.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0bdb71ea-a8dc-3b96-95c5-ae0909dd0269",
                        "entry_id": "916264f2-c5cb-3ed6-90d1-01bb514586cc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To scent so as to cover or conceal the original odour."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d690bcc9-1c17-4e74-9098-e8509c181b6d",
                                "sense_id": "0bdb71ea-a8dc-3b96-95c5-ae0909dd0269",
                                "text": "having the stinch of his railing tongue, over-sented with the fragrant ointment of this Prince’s memory"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4609ba3f-c28b-4401-a162-92e935db694e",
                                "sense_id": "0bdb71ea-a8dc-3b96-95c5-ae0909dd0269",
                                "text": "[…] she feels the truck moving toward her, rattling the small-town night with its rough bellow, close enough now to scrape the low-hanging branches and overscent the gentle lilacs,"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
